# 32-bit kernel serving the modern binder protocol (version 8).
# Apply IN ADDITION to binder.fragment for the 32-bit protocol-8 matrix entry:
# a 32-bit kernel whose userspace is 32-bit and speaks protocol 8, which is what
# every kernel from 4.18 serves and what a vendor BSP backporting a newer binder
# driver onto an older base serves too.
#
# The explicit disable is required, not cosmetic. On a 32-bit kernel at 4.17 or
# older the symbol exists and is `default y`, so leaving it unset here would
# yield protocol 7. binder.fragment can leave it unset only because its other
# variants are 64-bit, where `depends on !64BIT` makes the symbol unavailable.
# CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_32BIT is not set
